course: dictionary
lesson: 4015
title: Garment: a word for clothes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A garment is a piece of clothing. Shirts, dresses, coats and trousers are all garments. Shops, factories and labels often use this formal word instead of clothes. «Wash this garment inside out» is a label telling you how to look after a piece of clothing.
explain: Look at the words around garment to work out its meaning. «A garment factory» is a factory that makes clothes. «Outer garment» is a word for clothes you wear over the top, like a coat. To check, swap in the word clothes and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Rend your heart and not your garments» comes from the Bible (Joel 2:13). Rend means tear. In Bible times, sad people tore their clothes to show sorrow. The message is that sorrow should be felt inside, not just shown by torn clothes.
fact: A garment is a piece of clothing, such as a shirt, dress, coat or pair of trousers.
fact: Garment is a formal word, so you will often see it in shops, factories and on labels.
fact: «Garment care» means looking after clothes, for example by following the washing label.
fact: «Pyjamas», «shampoo» and «bungalow» all came into English from Hindi and Urdu during British rule in India.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word, and they can help you work out its meaning.
exercise: «Wash this garment inside out.» What is a garment? | A small bag | A type of shoe | *A piece of clothing | A kind of washing powder
exercise: In «a garment factory», what is made? | *Clothes | Toys | Bread | Cars
exercise: Which of these is a garment? | A spoon | A bicycle | *A shirt | A football
test: «Rend your heart and not your garments» uses garments to mean what? | Gloves | Games | *Clothes | Gardens
test: What does «outer garment» mean? | A type of tree | A letter sent by post | A small garden shed | *A coat or jacket worn over other clothes
exam: In «Rend your heart and not your garments», what is the message? | Tear your clothes whenever you feel happy | Clothes are not important at all | *Show sorrow inside, not just by tearing your clothes | Buy more garments for the church
